 the $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^0 K^0_S$ decay mode, observed through the $D^0\to K^-K^+$ decay sequence following $6.3$ femtobarns of proton-proton collisions accumulated by the LHCb detector at a centre-of-mass energy of 7, 8 and 9 TeV. The $B^0_s\to\bar{D}^0 \bar{K}^0$ branching fraction is determined to be $(4.3\pm 0.3\pm 0.2)\times 10^{-4}$ with a significance of 11 standard deviations, and the $C.P.$-violation parameter is found to be $0.206\pm 0.034\pm 0.006$. Furthermore, the $B^0_s\to D^{*0} \bar{K}^0$ decay mode is discovered using the $D^{*0}\to D^0\pi^0$ or $D^{*0}\to D^0\gamma$ transitions, with branching fractions calculated to be $(1.8\pm 0.3\pm 0.1)\times 10^{-3}$ and $(6.4\pm 1.0\pm 0.3)\times 10^{-4}$, respectively. The $C.P.$-violation parameters for $B^0_s\to D^{*0} \bar{K}^0$ decays are also measured for the two channels. The $D^{*0}$ modes significantly extend the reach of experimental $C.P.$-violation measurements in $B^0_s$ decays. 

